## Implemented Contract

Occurrence mapping:

- Generation-bearing `RenderOccurrenceId` and snapshot-local nonzero
  framebuffer token; zero remains background.
- Immutable shared snapshot binds authority, document revision, projection
  revision, scene, scene epoch, device generation, and mapping generation.
- Exact `(scene,node,primitive,instanceOrdinal)` keys distinguish definition
  reuse across nodes and instances.
- Node topology is sealed as a canonical parent/depth preorder. Unknown,
  duplicate, foreign, noncanonical ordinal, reused live slot, and capacity
  inputs fail before snapshot publication.
- Node highlight expands the sealed descendant preorder and filters effective
  hidden occurrences. Primitive highlight resolves exactly one occurrence.
- Factory failure messages are static `string_view` values. A deterministic
  allocation-fault hook proves `noexcept` returns `allocationFailure` without
  a partial snapshot or second allocation.

Picking types and producer:

- Full `EditorSceneFence` and `EditorPickFence`, monotonic request serial,
  single/double intent, attachment sample, normalized world ray, mapping
  generation, and closed hit/miss/error/cancelled terminal payloads.
- Accepted requests retain the exact immutable occurrence snapshot through
  physical readback retirement and terminal consumption.
- Backend enqueue/poll/cancel/retire is injected through MGIF logical RHI
  contracts. There is no synchronous wait or device-idle surface.
- Readback matches the exact `(ticket, SubmissionToken)` pair, preventing a
  late old readback from ABA-terminating a reused ticket.
- Malformed backend status/reason combinations normalize to a valid error or
  cancellation terminal; no accepted request is removed with an invalid
  terminal payload.
- A required, no-throw `IScenePickingTerminalSink` receives ready and pending
  terminals during zero-allocation destruction shutdown. Snapshot release
  occurs only after the sink callback.
- Duplicate/unknown late readbacks are ignored; exact queue submission tokens
  are retired once.

Shader:

- Vertex and fragment entrypoints write a snapshot-local unsigned token to
  `SV_Target0`.
- Renderer draw index remains private to draw-data lookup and is never treated
  as a document identity.
- Alpha-cutout discard is preserved.
- No native image/descriptor handle or stable document identifier is encoded.

